co-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Sample of content: the Credo's introduction — a pastoral apologetic for faith#{2}":[49,49],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Sample of content: the Credo's introduction — a pastoral apologetic for faith#{3}":[50,50],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Sample of content: the Credo's introduction — a pastoral apologetic for faith#{4}":[51,51],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Sample of content: the Credo's introduction — a pastoral apologetic for faith#{5}":[52,53],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Sample of content: the Credo's introduction — a pastoral apologetic for faith#{6}":[54,55],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Significance for this vault":[56,59],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Significance for this vault#{1}":[58,59],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Flagged for follow-up deep ingest":[60,63],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Flagged for follow-up deep ingest#{1}":[62,63],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Raw File":[64,67],"#Source: Opuscoli teologico-spirituali — the Naples Lenten sermons of 1273#Raw File#{1}":[66,67]},"outlinks":[{"title":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","target":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","line":13},{"title":"Tomismo","target":"Tomismo","line":14},{"title":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","target":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","line":58},{"title":"Tomismo","target":"Tomismo","line":58},{"title":"god-philosophy-universities","target":"god-philosophy-universities","line":62}],"metadata":{"type":"source","title":"Opuscoli teologico-spirituali (Le prediche di Napoli, 1273)","address":"c-000034","created":"2026-07-25","updated":"2026-07-25","tags":["#tomismo","#source","#primary-text"],"status":"developing","related":["[[San Tommaso d'Aquino]]","[[Tomismo]]"],"source_type":"book","author":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","date_published":"1273 (delivered); this printed edition n.d., Imprimatur Giovanni Canestri","url":"","confidence":"high","key_claims":["These four opuscula are stenographic records (by Fra Pietro da Andria and others) of Aquinas's last Lenten preaching cycle (Naples, 1273), delivered in vernacular to ordinary lay people and students, not in the technical Latin of university disputation.","Aquinas structures the whole cycle around the three theological virtues: the Creed answers what to believe (faith), the Our Father what to desire (hope), and the Decalogue/two precepts of charity what to do (charity).","In the Credo's introduction, Aquinas gives a pastoral, non-technical defense of the reasonableness of faith: the weakness of human intellect (no philosopher has ever fully understood a single fly), the necessity of trusting testimony in ordinary life, and miracles as God's authenticating 'seal' on revealed truth."],"raw_file":".raw/S. Tommaso d'Aquino - Opuscoli.pdf"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Wiki/sources/opuscoli-tommaso.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"1e5u866","at":1785014026854},"key":"Wiki/sources/opuscoli-tommaso.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,25],"size":1305,"outlinks":[{"title":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","target":"San Tommaso d'Aquino","line":13},{"title":"Tomismo","target":"Tomismo","line":14}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
